{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"ff808ade-d104-40d4-ba11-dbcf51198464","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box retired 8/14. Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\\\"sharpened, not soothed\\\").\\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: scroll-craft in. Build #1 `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, committed, UNPUSHED. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`: Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx prototypes, mock data. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: 08-14 set shipped (framework + Appendix A NCAA crosswalk, workflow, exec summary); old in `_Archive/`. Gaps: Education, Working Group, transfer-SA, consent template, annual survey. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory email.\\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: JD accepted; OKR v3 = semester cycles, Aug-31 closeout. Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. Ruf email (7 Qs) ready; Fri reports from 7/20. →SecondBrain JD-2026.\\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. `DEV/Kinexon_Volleyball` (private). Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\\n- **Open PRs**: CLIs #1667+#1668 green await merge; SpeedProfiling #9; KeystoneOS #17. Drafts: ForcePlate #2, cmj-traffic-light #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\\n- **Dormant**: Tezino CampPrep (6/17), FaceComps sim (LOCKED 6/15) →Tier A dormant-threads.\\n- **CLI lessons (8/16)**: `DEV/Terminal_Fluency` 01-03 done. OPEN: rotate Fireflies key. →Tier A terminal-fluency-workspace.\\n- **RTP CLA course (9/3)**: `DEV/RTP_Constraints_Course`: lesson 0001 shipped, MISSION final. Scans p014–p101 `~/Downloads/vFlat/iPhone 15/`; **more 9/4, resume p102**. Myszka emailed 9/3 (his PDF → stop scanning). NEXT: Joe lesson + Parry PDF (CA2CRR6Z). →Tier A book-scan-page-ordering.\\n- **Child dental (6/25)**: 4yo cavities. NEXT: ped. dentist, SDF/n-HAp.\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- **Portfolio dashboard** LIVE: `DEV/project-triage/portfolio.json`; `/project` re-renders+republishes; pulse.md→briefing.\\n- Schedules, gws/Gmail limits →Tier A automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon-anchored, 8/24–1/23) →Tier A cfb-forecast-capture.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **DUE (was 8/31)**: OKR Q1 gate: re-evaluate AI integration (buy-in) + data governance (Anthony's proposal).\\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink intros (~half Kitman's cost) while buying Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4600 chars, updated 2026-09-04 11:29)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":508},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c3a1995f-4e43-44db-bec5-ba812ad6f60f","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:33:09.317Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"c3a1995f-4e43-44db-bec5-ba812ad6f60f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"ff808ade-d104-40d4-ba11-dbcf51198464","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nFriday, September 04, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n229 compiled articles (173 concepts, 55 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n### Memory Flush (07:26)\\n\\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\\n\\n### Memory Flush (07:26)\\n\\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\\n\\n### Session (07:31)\\n\\n**Context:** Setting up faster tmux window creation inside the VS Code integrated terminal on macOS.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- Asked for the fast way to open a new terminal window with tmux in VS Code. Answer: `Ctrl+b` then `c` \\u2014 but VS Code intercepts `Ctrl+b` for sidebar toggle before tmux receives it.\\n- Two options presented: (A) tell VS Code to skip the binding, or (B) remap the tmux prefix to `Ctrl+a` in `~/.tmux.conf`.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Chose option A \\u2014 added `\\\"terminal.integrated.commandsToSkipShell\\\": [\\\"-workbench.action.toggleSidebarVisibility\\\"]` to VS Code `settings.json`. Rationale: one-line change, keeps the default tmux prefix so online tmux docs/guides match his keys without translation.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- VS Code's `terminal.integrated.commandsToSkipShell` accepts a `-` prefix on a command ID to *remove* it from the skip list, letting the keystroke pass through to the shell/tmux instead of being consumed by the editor.\\n- The `Ctrl+b` collision between tmux prefix and VS Code sidebar toggle is the standard gotcha when running tmux in the integrated terminal.\\n- No VS Code restart needed; the setting applies immediately.\\n\\n**Files Changed:**\\n- `/Users/kristinarash/Library/Application Support/Code/User/settings.json` (backup written to `settings.json.bak-20260904` in same folder)\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Verify `Ctrl+b` + `c` creates a tmux window and no longer toggles the sidebar; if the sidebar still hides, reload the VS Code window.\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":511},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e04dd9b3-97c3-44e5-8671-ce019b319847","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:33:09.318Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"e04dd9b3-97c3-44e5-8671-ce019b319847","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"ff808ade-d104-40d4-ba11-dbcf51198464","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":510},"type":"attachment","uuid":"861f47aa-16d2-4836-b8a1-db854b34f72c","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:33:09.318Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"861f47aa-16d2-4836-b8a1-db854b34f72c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"ff808ade-d104-40d4-ba11-dbcf51198464","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"/last30days: Ready to use. Run /last30days to get started — setup takes 30 seconds.\n  Research any topic across Reddit, HN, X, YouTube, Polymarket (last 30 days).\n\nReddit, Hacker News, Polymarket, and YouTube (yt-dlp detected) work out of the box.\nThe setup wizard can unlock X/Twitter and more.\n  Detected: yt-dlp is installed (YouTube transcripts ready, no setup needed).","stdout":"/last30days: Ready to use. Run /last30days to get started — setup takes 30 seconds.\n  Research any topic across Reddit, HN, X, YouTube, Polymarket (last 30 days).\n\nReddit, Hacker News, Polymarket, and YouTube (yt-dlp detected) work out of the box.\nThe setup wizard can unlock X/Twitter and more.\n  Detected: yt-dlp is installed (YouTube transcripts ready, no setup needed).\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"bash \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${extensionPath:-.}}/hooks/scripts/check-config.sh\"","durationMs":752},"type":"attachment","uuid":"45283672-c988-4f2e-a751-99bd9057824c","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:33:09.560Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"45283672-c988-4f2e-a751-99bd9057824c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"ff808ade-d104-40d4-ba11-dbcf51198464","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n    \"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\",\n    \"additionalContext\": \"<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\\nYou have superpowers.\\n\\n**Below is the full content of your 'superpowers:using-superpowers' skill - your introduction to using skills. For all other skills, use the 'Skill' tool:**\\n\\n---\\nname: using-superpowers\\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring skill invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\\n---\\n\\n<SUBAGENT-STOP>\\nIf you were dispatched as a subagent to execute a specific task, ignore this skill.\\n</SUBAGENT-STOP>\\n\\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\\n\\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\\n\\nThis is not negotiable. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\\n\\n## The Rule\\n\\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action** — including clarifying questions, exploring the codebase, or checking files. If it turns out wrong for the situation, you don't have to use it.\\n\\n**Before entering plan mode:** if you haven't already brainstormed, invoke the brainstorming skill first.\\n\\nThen announce \\\"Using [skill] to [purpose]\\\" and follow the skill exactly. If it has a checklist, create a todo per item.\\n\\n## Skill Priority\\n\\nWhen multiple skills apply, process skills come first — they set the approach, then implementation skills (frontend-design, etc.) carry it out. Brainstorming and systematic-debugging are Superpowers' most common process skills, but the rule holds for any of them.\\n\\n- \\\"Let's build X\\\" → superpowers:brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\\n- \\\"Fix this bug\\\" → superpowers:systematic-debugging first, then domain skills.\\n\\n## Red Flags\\n\\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\\n\\n| Thought | Reality |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| \\\"This is just a simple question\\\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"I need more context first\\\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\\n| \\\"Let me explore the codebase first\\\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\\n| \\\"I can check git/files quickly\\\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"Let me gather information first\\\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\\n| \\\"This doesn't need a formal skill\\\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\\n| \\\"I remember this skill\\\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\\n| \\\"This doesn't count as a task\\\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"The skill is overkill\\\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\\n| \\\"I'll just do this one thing first\\\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\\n| \\\"This feels productive\\\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\\n| \\\"I know what that means\\\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\\n\\n## Platform Adaptation\\n\\nIf your harness appears here, read its reference file for special instructions:\\n\\n- Codex: `references/codex-tools.md`\\n- Pi: `references/pi-tools.md`\\n- Antigravity: `references/antigravity-tools.md`\\n- Hermes Agent: `references/hermes-tools.md`\\n\\n## User Instructions\\n\\nUser instructions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, etc, direct requests) take precedence over skills, which in turn override default behavior. Only skip skill workflows or instructions when your human partner has explicitly told you to.\\n</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\"\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/run-hook.cmd\" session-start","durationMs":752},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5bc37307-d1e4-47f9-ae0b-990f77367613","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:33:09.561Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
