{"parentUuid":"e9019e22-5413-47a9-8792-59242f70ef8c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e59b4284-645a-4b92-99bd-890450acae7d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018pUbpfebtpZTr2oTwyyhsL","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: vendored-skill-install\ndescription: \"Installing a third-party skill so Claude Code, Codex and Cowork can all use it — the canonical store, the two symlinks, the CLI flag trap, and why Cowork is different\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:11.845Z\n---\n\nThird-party skills live in **`~/.agents/skills/<name>/`** (the real files, ~360 of\nthem) with `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` as the install ledger. Both harness\ndirectories are symlinks into it:\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/<name>` → `../../.agents/skills/<name>` (relative)\n- `~/.codex/skills/<name>` → absolute path into `~/.agents/skills/`\n\nInstall with the CLI that owns that store, not by hand-copying:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y skills@latest add <owner>/<repo> -g -a claude-code -a codex -s <skill> -y\n```\n\n**Trap: `-a` will not take a comma-separated list.** `-a claude-code,codex`\nfails with \"Invalid agents: claude-code,codex\" and then prints a valid-agent\nlist containing both names. Repeat the flag instead.\n\n**Trap: the installer does not always wire Codex.** It reports\n`universal: Codex` and creates no symlink. Check\n`ls -l ~/.codex/skills/<name>` after every install and make the symlink by hand\nif it is missing.\n\nThe CLI runs a security scan and may report alerts. Read\n`https://skills.sh/<owner>/<repo>` before trusting a skill.\n\n**Cowork cannot take a locally-dropped skill.** Its store is\n`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/<a>/<b>/skills/`\nwith a sibling `manifest.json`, and every entry carries a **server-minted id**\n(`skill_01…`). A folder placed there is not in the manifest and is wiped on the\nnext sync. The only route is a zip uploaded through claude.ai → Settings →\nCapabilities → Skills, with the skill folder at the zip root. Expect Cowork's\nsandbox to lack ffmpeg/Chrome, so any skill's verification or media step will\nnot run there even after a successful upload.\n\nWhere a skill puts its *output* is separate: some resolve a workspace from the\nnearest `.git` walking up, so run them from inside the target project or set\ntheir env override, or builds land wherever cwd happened to be.\n\nSee [[vendored-skill-repair]] for what to do when one of these is broken, and\n[[path-shadowing-and-cleanup]] before deleting any copy.\n=== REPAIR ===\n---\nname: vendored-skill-repair\ndescription: \"A vendored skill fails silently or with a confusing error — check for removed ffmpeg flags first, patch every live copy, and expect the fix to revert on update\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:23.955Z\n---\n\nWhen a third-party skill produces **empty output rather than an error**, suspect\na CLI flag the underlying tool has since removed, not the skill's own logic.\n\n**The instance (2026-09-02):** `/watch` returned zero frames with no useful\nmessage. Cause: `frames.py` passed ffmpeg `-vsync`, removed in ffmpeg 7+. This\nmachine runs **ffmpeg 9.0.1**. Fix is `-vsync` → `-fps_mode` (same `vfr` value,\nsame position, exists since ffmpeg 5.0).\n\n**Patch every live copy, and know which ones matter.** A skill can exist three\ntimes on this machine:\n\n1. `~/.agents/skills/<name>/…` — the vendor store, serves `~/.claude/skills/` and Codex.\n2. `~/.claude/plugins/cache/<plugin>/<skill>/<version>/skills/<name>/…` — the\n   plugin copy. **This is the one a `/slash` invocation actually loads.** Patch\n   only the vendor store and the skill stays broken.\n3. The Cowork copy under `Library/Application Support/Claude/…` — **do not\n   patch.** It is server-synced and reverts. See [[vendored-skill-install]].\n\nConfirm which file is live by reading the \"Base directory for this skill\" line\nthe harness prints when the skill loads.\n\n**Every such patch is temporary.** Check upstream before assuming a fix is\nneeded, and after patching, assume `skills update` or a plugin update reinstalls\nthe bug. For `/watch` the upstream is `bradautomates/claude-video`, still\ncarrying `-vsync` as of its 2026-06-30 commit.\n\nVerify by running the affected code path and **counting the output**, not by\nreading the exit code — the original failure exited 0.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cf1070f0-8df3-484b-8c5d-6cf474ac6517","timestamp":"2026-09-04T12:49:53.234Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: vendored-skill-install\ndescription: \"Installing a third-party skill so Claude Code, Codex and Cowork can all use it — the canonical store, the two symlinks, the CLI flag trap, and why Cowork is different\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:11.845Z\n---\n\nThird-party skills live in **`~/.agents/skills/<name>/`** (the real files, ~360 of\nthem) with `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` as the install ledger. Both harness\ndirectories are symlinks into it:\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/<name>` → `../../.agents/skills/<name>` (relative)\n- `~/.codex/skills/<name>` → absolute path into `~/.agents/skills/`\n\nInstall with the CLI that owns that store, not by hand-copying:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y skills@latest add <owner>/<repo> -g -a claude-code -a codex -s <skill> -y\n```\n\n**Trap: `-a` will not take a comma-separated list.** `-a claude-code,codex`\nfails with \"Invalid agents: claude-code,codex\" and then prints a valid-agent\nlist containing both names. Repeat the flag instead.\n\n**Trap: the installer does not always wire Codex.** It reports\n`universal: Codex` and creates no symlink. Check\n`ls -l ~/.codex/skills/<name>` after every install and make the symlink by hand\nif it is missing.\n\nThe CLI runs a security scan and may report alerts. Read\n`https://skills.sh/<owner>/<repo>` before trusting a skill.\n\n**Cowork cannot take a locally-dropped skill.** Its store is\n`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/<a>/<b>/skills/`\nwith a sibling `manifest.json`, and every entry carries a **server-minted id**\n(`skill_01…`). A folder placed there is not in the manifest and is wiped on the\nnext sync. The only route is a zip uploaded through claude.ai → Settings →\nCapabilities → Skills, with the skill folder at the zip root. Expect Cowork's\nsandbox to lack ffmpeg/Chrome, so any skill's verification or media step will\nnot run there even after a successful upload.\n\nWhere a skill puts its *output* is separate: some resolve a workspace from the\nnearest `.git` walking up, so run them from inside the target project or set\ntheir env override, or builds land wherever cwd happened to be.\n\nSee [[vendored-skill-repair]] for what to do when one of these is broken, and\n[[path-shadowing-and-cleanup]] before deleting any copy.\n=== REPAIR ===\n---\nname: vendored-skill-repair\ndescription: \"A vendored skill fails silently or with a confusing error — check for removed ffmpeg flags first, patch every live copy, and expect the fix to revert on update\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:23.955Z\n---\n\nWhen a third-party skill produces **empty output rather than an error**, suspect\na CLI flag the underlying tool has since removed, not the skill's own logic.\n\n**The instance (2026-09-02):** `/watch` returned zero frames with no useful\nmessage. Cause: `frames.py` passed ffmpeg `-vsync`, removed in ffmpeg 7+. This\nmachine runs **ffmpeg 9.0.1**. Fix is `-vsync` → `-fps_mode` (same `vfr` value,\nsame position, exists since ffmpeg 5.0).\n\n**Patch every live copy, and know which ones matter.** A skill can exist three\ntimes on this machine:\n\n1. `~/.agents/skills/<name>/…` — the vendor store, serves `~/.claude/skills/` and Codex.\n2. `~/.claude/plugins/cache/<plugin>/<skill>/<version>/skills/<name>/…` — the\n   plugin copy. **This is the one a `/slash` invocation actually loads.** Patch\n   only the vendor store and the skill stays broken.\n3. The Cowork copy under `Library/Application Support/Claude/…` — **do not\n   patch.** It is server-synced and reverts. See [[vendored-skill-install]].\n\nConfirm which file is live by reading the \"Base directory for this skill\" line\nthe harness prints when the skill loads.\n\n**Every such patch is temporary.** Check upstream before assuming a fix is\nneeded, and after patching, assume `skills update` or a plugin update reinstalls\nthe bug. For `/watch` the upstream is `bradautomates/claude-video`, still\ncarrying `-vsync` as of its 2026-06-30 commit.\n\nVerify by running the affected code path and **counting the output**, not by\nreading the exit code — the original failure exited 0.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e9019e22-5413-47a9-8792-59242f70ef8c","session_id":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
