{"parentUuid":"0839da0b-31bb-43d1-8619-0242081497ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9cec2abc-1cb1-43b5-be66-6927adbdb1a1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015LaoyUE8zmiW1FNC49iFwH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: vendored-skill-install\n3\tdescription: \"Installing a third-party skill so Claude Code, Codex and Cowork can all use it — the canonical store, the two symlinks, the CLI flag trap, and why Cowork is different\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:11.845Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tThird-party skills live in **`~/.agents/skills/<name>/`** (the real files, ~360 of\n12\tthem) with `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` as the install ledger. Both harness\n13\tdirectories are symlinks into it:\n14\t\n15\t- `~/.claude/skills/<name>` → `../../.agents/skills/<name>` (relative)\n16\t- `~/.codex/skills/<name>` → absolute path into `~/.agents/skills/`\n17\t\n18\tInstall with the CLI that owns that store, not by hand-copying:\n19\t\n20\t```bash\n21\tnpx -y skills@latest add <owner>/<repo> -g -a claude-code -a codex -s <skill> -y\n22\t```\n23\t\n24\t**Trap: `-a` will not take a comma-separated list.** `-a claude-code,codex`\n25\tfails with \"Invalid agents: claude-code,codex\" and then prints a valid-agent\n26\tlist containing both names. Repeat the flag instead.\n27\t\n28\t**Trap: the installer does not always wire Codex.** It reports\n29\t`universal: Codex` and creates no symlink. Check\n30\t`ls -l ~/.codex/skills/<name>` after every install and make the symlink by hand\n31\tif it is missing.\n32\t\n33\tThe CLI runs a security scan and may report alerts. Read\n34\t`https://skills.sh/<owner>/<repo>` before trusting a skill.\n35\t\n36\t**Cowork cannot take a locally-dropped skill.** Its store is\n37\t`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/<a>/<b>/skills/`\n38\twith a sibling `manifest.json`, and every entry carries a **server-minted id**\n39\t(`skill_01…`). A folder placed there is not in the manifest and is wiped on the\n40\tnext sync. The only route is a zip uploaded through claude.ai → Settings →\n41\tCapabilities → Skills, with the skill folder at the zip root. Expect Cowork's\n42\tsandbox to lack ffmpeg/Chrome, so any skill's verification or media step will\n43\tnot run there even after a successful upload.\n44\t\n45\tWhere a skill puts its *output* is separate: some resolve a workspace from the\n46\tnearest `.git` walking up, so run them from inside the target project or set\n47\ttheir env override, or builds land wherever cwd happened to be.\n48\t\n49\tSee [[vendored-skill-repair]] for what to do when one of these is broken, and\n50\t[[path-shadowing-and-cleanup]] before deleting any copy.\n51\t"}]},"uuid":"5928944f-6df5-4d59-ab04-483b253fab15","timestamp":"2026-09-04T13:43:07.305Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_vendored-skill-install.md","content":"---\nname: vendored-skill-install\ndescription: \"Installing a third-party skill so Claude Code, Codex and Cowork can all use it — the canonical store, the two symlinks, the CLI flag trap, and why Cowork is different\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: a6dfb3da-c339-44b1-a836-2a6884e07ea6\n  modified: 2026-09-02T23:05:11.845Z\n---\n\nThird-party skills live in **`~/.agents/skills/<name>/`** (the real files, ~360 of\nthem) with `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json` as the install ledger. Both harness\ndirectories are symlinks into it:\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/<name>` → `../../.agents/skills/<name>` (relative)\n- `~/.codex/skills/<name>` → absolute path into `~/.agents/skills/`\n\nInstall with the CLI that owns that store, not by hand-copying:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y skills@latest add <owner>/<repo> -g -a claude-code -a codex -s <skill> -y\n```\n\n**Trap: `-a` will not take a comma-separated list.** `-a claude-code,codex`\nfails with \"Invalid agents: claude-code,codex\" and then prints a valid-agent\nlist containing both names. Repeat the flag instead.\n\n**Trap: the installer does not always wire Codex.** It reports\n`universal: Codex` and creates no symlink. Check\n`ls -l ~/.codex/skills/<name>` after every install and make the symlink by hand\nif it is missing.\n\nThe CLI runs a security scan and may report alerts. Read\n`https://skills.sh/<owner>/<repo>` before trusting a skill.\n\n**Cowork cannot take a locally-dropped skill.** Its store is\n`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/local-agent-mode-sessions/skills-plugin/<a>/<b>/skills/`\nwith a sibling `manifest.json`, and every entry carries a **server-minted id**\n(`skill_01…`). A folder placed there is not in the manifest and is wiped on the\nnext sync. The only route is a zip uploaded through claude.ai → Settings →\nCapabilities → Skills, with the skill folder at the zip root. Expect Cowork's\nsandbox to lack ffmpeg/Chrome, so any skill's verification or media step will\nnot run there even after a successful upload.\n\nWhere a skill puts its *output* is separate: some resolve a workspace from the\nnearest `.git` walking up, so run them from inside the target project or set\ntheir env override, or builds land wherever cwd happened to be.\n\nSee [[vendored-skill-repair]] for what to do when one of these is broken, and\n[[path-shadowing-and-cleanup]] before deleting any copy.\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0839da0b-31bb-43d1-8619-0242081497ee","session_id":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"7792a3d6-362f-4bf0-95af-fbf3fcbe46f5","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
